          %h2#idea Idea
          %blockquote
            %p This section is no good…
          %p
            Any pretriangulated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            presents a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable (infinity,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            on each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
            to produce a fibrant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-enriched+category"} sSet-enriched category
            and then, if desired, form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
            of that to obtain a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
          %p
            On the other hand, the
            %em dg-nerve
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a more direct construction that directly sends the dg-category to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            incarnation of the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
          %p
            To the extent that one may think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            as analogous to a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            whose
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+systems"} local systems
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^k
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+%E2%88%9E-connections"} flat ∞-connections
            with coefficients in
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebroids"} L-infinity algebroids
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#CompatibilityWithSimplicialNerve Compatibility with the simplicial nerve
          %p Recall:
          %p
          #QuasiCategoricalLocalization.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              From a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+category"} relative category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \mathrm{W})
              (a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} W
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{W} \subset Mor(\mathcal{C})
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-enriched+category"} sSet-enriched category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} W
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}[\mathrm{W}^{-1}]
                  which is its
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
                  which is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} W
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \mathcal{C}[\mathrm{W}^{-1}]
                  of that.
            %p
              or alternatively, up to
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+quasi-categories"} equivalence of quasi-categories
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+nerve"} simplicial nerve
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+quasi-category"} localization as a quasi-category
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} W
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N\mathcal{C}[\mathrm{W}^{-1}]
            %p
          %p Now:
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ch
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
                  for the plain
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒜
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Ch
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Ch}_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
                  obtained form the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} self-enrichment
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ch
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
                %p
                  (via its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
                  structure given by the
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} W
                          %mi che
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Ch
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{W}_{che} \,\subset\, Mor\big(Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})\big)
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homotopy+equivalences"} chain homotopy equivalences
                %p
                  (which for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mo =
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A} = k
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
                  coincide with the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
            %p
              Then the dg-nerve of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Ch}_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+quasi-categories"} equivalent as a quasi-category
              to the (homotopy coherent) nerve of the (simplicial) localization of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
              at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} W
                      %mi che
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{W}_{che}
              in the sense of Rem.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuasiCategoricalLocalization"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi dg
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi N
                    %msub
